// ============================================================================
// poisson-cdf.epher -- cumulative Poisson probabilities with poissoncdf
//
// Calls arrive at a switchboard at a mean rate of 2 per minute, so the
// number X of calls in a minute is Poisson(2) and the chance of at most
// k calls is the cumulative probability P(X <= k), which epher's
// poissoncdf(k, rate) builtin sums from the point formula e^-rate *
// rate^j / j!. The builtin prints floats with tiny noise around the
// last digit.
//
// The script checks P(X <= 2) against the hand-written sum
// e^-2 * (1 + 2 + 2) = 5 * e^-2, and reads off the complementary tail
// P(X >= 3) = 1 - P(X <= 2): with only 0.323 of minutes carrying three
// or more calls, the operator is usually free.
//
// Source: Ross, "A First Course in Probability", chapter 4.
//
// Run it from a terminal:  epher "epher scripts/probability/distributions/poisson-cdf.epher"
// Web/desktop:             paste the file into the entry, press Enter
//
// The knob to edit is `rate`; everything below it is machinery.
// ============================================================================

// ---- the knob ----
const rate = 2

// ---- results ----
// At most two calls in a minute, from the builtin and from the sum of
// the first three point terms, e^-2 * (1 + 2 + 2^2/2!).
print("poissoncdf(2, 2):", poissoncdf(2, rate))
print("hand sum 5 * e^-2:", exp(-2) * 5)

// The tail: three or more calls in the minute.
print("P(X >= 3):", 1 - poissoncdf(2, rate))

// Larger windows: at most 4 calls covers about 95% of minutes, and at
// most 8 calls almost all of them.
print("P(X <= 4):", poissoncdf(4, rate))
print("P(X <= 8):", poissoncdf(8, rate))

// The Poisson distribution has mean equal to variance, both `rate`:
// about 2 calls per minute, with spread sqrt(2) = 1.414.
print("mean and variance:", rate)
print("standard deviation:", sqrt(rate))
// ---- expected output ----
// = 2
// = poissoncdf(2, 2): 0.67667641619
// = hand sum 5 * e^-2: 0.676676416183
// = P(X >= 3): 0.32332358381
// = P(X <= 4): 0.947346982668
// = P(X <= 8): 0.999762552684
// = mean and variance: 2
// = standard deviation: 1.41421356237
